{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> Because he mentioned the night of watching, and it is the night of the fifteenth, in which the Paschal offering is eaten, he proceeded to explain the statute of the Paschal offering for generations. Now he did not mention the matter of the lintel and the doorpost, nor did he mention unleavened bread and bitter herbs, for he had already mentioned them in the Paschal offering of Egypt. Now the reason is: you shall eat the Paschal offering for generations like the Paschal offering of Egypt, and he added other commandments; only the commandment of the lintel and the doorpost is not of the matter of eating the Paschal offering. Behold, you will see at the beginning of the pericope: every foreigner shall not eat of it — and the reason is like \"of it,\" for it is sound in the sacred language, also in the Arabic language, to say thus; and like it: and that which remains of the flesh and of the bread (Leviticus 8:32)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:59.540140978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}